  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5e2857ba-a449-4922-97dc-b447f2f480cd",
    "name": "TutorCruncher Agents Clients API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "REST API for TutorCruncher, tutoring business management software for agencies, companies, and independent tutors. The API exposes the core domain - clients, recipients (students), contractors (tutors), agents, services (jobs), appointments (lessons), invoices, payment orders, proforma invoices, ad hoc charges, and reference data - plus HTTP webhooks for event notifications.\nBase URL: https://app.tutorcruncher.com/api/. Authentication uses a private API key (found under Integrations) sent in the Authorization header as `token <API KEY>`. All list endpoints are paginated with up to 100 objects per page and return `count`, `next`, `previous`, and `results`. Requests are rate limited to 100 per minute. This document targets API v2 (v1 was deprecated 2025-07-03); in v2, users are updated by ID (for example `POST /api/clients/{id}/`) rather than by email.\nNote: TutorCruncher's \"Socket\" is a JavaScript embed (https://cdn.tutorcruncher.com/socket/latest/socket.js) for publishing public tutor and lesson listings on a website; it is not a WebSocket API and is not modeled here. Event delivery is via HTTP webhooks.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: TutorCruncher",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
